cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "triage-pg: early-warning ML pipelines native to PostgreSQL"
abstract: >-
  triage-pg builds temporal machine-learning pipelines for tabular
  public-policy data — cohort, labels, features, matrices, train, predict,
  evaluate — with point-in-time correctness enforced by construction.
  Predictions are append-only and evaluation (precision@k, recall@k, AUC,
  regression and survival metrics, leaderboards, audition and bias group-bys)
  runs as SQL inside the database, so results are queryable without leaving
  PostgreSQL. It runs on plain PostgreSQL with no proprietary extensions. It
  is a deliberately simplified rewrite of DSSG triage, keeping that project's
  pipeline shape and its timechop temporal-splitting component.
type: software
authors:
